{"id":55573,"ord":25,"n_segments":90,"prev":55572,"next":55574,"doc":{"id":"68090","title":"68090_Ed Garland oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Ed Garland","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68090/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68090"},"chapter":"California: Oliver, Ory and the 111","title":"The 1921 King Oliver band on the West Coast","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Garland lists the personnel of Oliver's 1921 band, which played nightclubs and shows from arrangements.","period":"1921","year_from":1921,"year_to":1921,"words":225,"start":[41,2],"end":[42,16],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68090#s55573","tags":{"places":[{"name":"West Coast","focus":1,"type":"region"}],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"King Oliver's band","focus":1,"leader":"King Oliver"}]},"people":[{"name":"King Oliver","qid":"Q313368","n":9},{"name":"Dave (mellophone, Oliver band)","qid":null,"n":3},{"name":"Ed Garland","qid":"Q1282347","n":2},{"name":"Johnny Dodds","qid":"Q498495","n":1},{"name":"Ram Hall","qid":"Q1555744","n":1},{"name":"Jimmy Palao","qid":"Q14639678","n":1},{"name":"Payton","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Honore Dutrey","qid":"Q376220","n":1},{"name":"Lil Hardin","qid":"Q462562","n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":41,"b":2,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"That's great. And then so you go in 1921 to the West Coast."},{"p":41,"b":3,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Right. That's when we all come back together with Joe, you know."},{"p":41,"b":4,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Right."},{"p":41,"b":5,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"We all got together."},{"p":41,"b":6,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Who was in that band, Tootie, Tudi the Oliver band then, in 1921, who was playing with the King then?"},{"p":41,"b":7,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Let's see. The Great King Oliver."},{"p":41,"b":8,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Who played in that band with you?"},{"p":41,"b":9,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"King Oliver?"},{"p":41,"b":10,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah. In 1921."},{"p":41,"b":11,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Oh, in '21?"},{"p":41,"b":12,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":41,"b":13,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"When we come to the coast?"},{"p":41,"b":14,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah. Who was in that band?"},{"p":41,"b":15,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"I'll tell you. Let's see, I'll start from the piano. Little. L'il Little Hardin."},{"p":41,"b":16,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Right."},{"p":41,"b":17,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"On the piano. Johnny Dodds on the clarinet. Minor Myer Hall on the trombone. I mean, the drums."},{"p":41,"b":18,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Drums. Right."},{"p":41,"b":19,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Dave -- Dave --"},{"p":42,"b":0,"s":"","x":"HEMLOCK"},{"p":42,"b":1,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"Payton?"},{"p":42,"b":2,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"No, Dave -- Dave -- Dave -- played a mellophone and alto saxophone. Jimmy Palao played tenor saxophone and violin."},{"p":42,"b":3,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":42,"b":4,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"I was on the boss. Honore Dutroy played trombone. (Unintelligible). Dave (Unintelligible)."},{"p":42,"b":5,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"I see. Uh-huh. And you're still playing music, no arrangements, everything --"},{"p":42,"b":6,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"No. Joe had arrangements."},{"p":42,"b":7,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"Joe had arrangements. Uh-huh."},{"p":42,"b":8,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"Yeah. Joe had arrangements."},{"p":42,"b":9,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"And what were you playing, for dances or nightclubs then?"},{"p":42,"b":10,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"Yeah. Nightclubs."},{"p":42,"b":11,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"Nightclubs. Okay."},{"p":42,"b":12,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"Entertainments."},{"p":42,"b":13,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"I see. So you played shows, too, at the same time."},{"p":42,"b":14,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"We played shows, yeah."},{"p":42,"b":15,"s":"MR. TURETSKY:","x":"I see. Uh-huh. Was Joe a reading player?"},{"p":42,"b":16,"s":"MR. GARLAND:","x":"Yeah, Joe read he was."}]}